==Latin==

===Etymology===
From {{der|la|itc-pro|*auti}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*h₂ewti|t=on the other hand}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*h₂ew}}. Cognate with {{m|la|autem}}, {{cog|grc|αὖ}}, {{m|grc|αὖτε}}, {{m|grc|αὐτός}}, {{m|grc|αὐτάρ}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA}}

===Conjunction===
{{head|la|conjunction}}

# [[or]]
#: {{ux|la|'''Aut''' Caesar '''aut''' nihil.|All '''or''' nothing.|lit='''Either''' a Caesar '''or''' a nothing.|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|la|'''Aut''' disce '''aut''' discēde.|'''Either''' you learn, '''or''' go away.|inline=1}}
#* {{Q|la|Livy|Ab Urbe Condita|3|16|4|quote=nemo tribunos '''aut''' plebem timebat|t=nobody feared the tribunes '''or''' the plebs}}
#* {{Q|la|Jerome|Vulgate|Tobiae|3|19|quote={{...}}et '''aut''' ego indigna fuī illīs '''aut''' illī mihi forsitan dignī nōn fuērunt.|t={{...}}and '''either''' I was unworthy for them, '''or''' they perhaps were not worthy for me.}}
# [[otherwise]], [[or else]] {{gl|a consequence of the condition that the previous is false}}
#: {{ux|la|Accipe nummōs nōnāgintā — '''aut''' nūllōs!|Take 90 sesterces — '''or''' none at all!|ref=<ref>{{cite-book|last=Oerberg|first=Hans H.|url=https://www.worldcat.org/oclc/701808086|title=Lingua Latina per se illustrata. Pars I, Familia Romana|year=2011|page=58|isbn=978-1-58510-423-9|location=Newburyport, MA|oclc=701808086}}</ref>}}
# {{n-g|Introduces a correction to the previous words or an afterthought remark.}}

====Usage notes====
* {{sense|or}} Equivalent to “{{l|en|either}} … {{l|en|or}}” when placed before each coordinated element (“{{l|la|aut}} … {{l|la|aut}}”).

